-- title:
--   Base change of a two-chart integral model is the glued curve
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure and $j \in F$ a nonzero element; let $K$ be a field which is an $R$-algebra, $L$ a field extension of $K$ and $t \in L$ nonzero. Write $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $\mathcal O_{\infty} =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the elements integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$; likewise `CurveModel.chartRing K {t}` and `CurveModel.chartRing K {t⁻¹}` are the subalgebras of $L$ of elements integral over $K[t]$, resp. $K[t^{-1}]$. Assume given $K$-algebra isomorphisms $e_{\mathrm{fin}} : K \otimes_R \mathcal O_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \overline{K[t]}$ and $e_{\infty} : K \otimes_R \mathcal O_{\infty} \to \overline{K[t^{-1}]}$ such that $e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes j) = t$ and $e_{\infty}(1 \otimes j^{-1}) = t^{-1}$ as elements of $L$, and such that the compatibility holds: for all $b \in \mathcal O_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $b' \in \mathcal O_{\infty}$ and all $n \in \mathbb N$, if $b = b' j^{n}$ in $F$ then $e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes b) = e_{\infty}(1 \otimes b')\, t^{n}$ in $L$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a morphism $es$ from `CurveModel.glued K t`, the scheme obtained by gluing $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{K[t]}$ and $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{K[t^{-1}]}$ along the overlap chart, to the fibre product of `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase R F j` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to K$, together with the assertion that $es$ is an isomorphism, subject to three identities: $es$ followed by the second projection equals `CurveModel.gluedToBase K t`; and, for each of the two charts, the chart immersion (`CurveModel.ι₀ K t`, resp. `CurveModel.ιInf K t`) followed by $es$ and then by the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring homomorphism $b \mapsto e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes b)$ (resp. $b' \mapsto e_{\infty}(1 \otimes b')$) followed by the corresponding chart immersion `TwoChartIntegralModel.ιFin R F j` (resp. `TwoChartIntegralModel.ιInf R F j`).
--
--   This is the statement that base change commutes with the two-chart gluing: the fibre over $\operatorname{Spec} K$ of the two-chart integral model of $(F,j)$ over $R$ is identified, chart by chart and compatibly with the structure morphisms, with the glued curve attached to $(L,t)$ over $K$. It is used in the variant hypothesised on a fraction-field condition, and through that in the construction of curve models for the modular curves $X_1(p)$ and related quotients.
